{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And for all</b> the children of Israel there was light, etc. He was precise in saying <b>and for all</b>, to say that each and every one of Israel who would go to an Egyptian's house had light in the Egyptians' dwellings." "Or it may intend to say: this light — whence did it come forth? And he said that it was <b>light in their dwellings</b>, and the word 'אשר' is lacking, and many verses abbreviate thus. And the intent, according to the way of our Sages of blessed memory (Exodus Rabbah 14:2), is that the wicked are covered by darkness — and it was this that covered the wicked Egyptians — whereas corresponding to the righteous, upon them may HaShem blessed be He shine, and His beloved are like the sun going forth in its might. And from the light of their dwellings HaShem blessed be He accompanied them with one portion, and this is what He said: <b>light in their dwellings</b>."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:26.117958356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}